(I'm not sure I understand the intention of your question completely.
A few remarks anyway...)

Bashing means contact, wands avoid contact; but missiles avoid combat as
well as attack spells. So my precedence is (if applicable for the specific
race/role/equipment/game); first ranged attacks (physical or spell), then
melee. In exceptional or specific cases ranged attack wands.

In my experience wands for offensive purposes are rarely the first choice
for combat. Exceptions are the wand of death (for the Wizard and two of
the Riders). Specifically fire and lightning I consider and use primarily
as defensive wands. This is my choice for all game phases (though in the
early game of some game instance I may have to deviate from that principle).

